Brief info about Vinted&nbsp;

Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we're looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life - or even a third.
The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:

Vinted Marketplace is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.

Vinted Go enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.

Vinted Pay is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.

Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania's first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we've grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&nbsp;

About Vinted Go

Vinted, headquartered in Vilnius, Lithuania, is Europe’s leading online C2C marketplace dedicated to second-hand fashion. With Vinted Go, launched in 2022, we are expanding our focus to develop innovative shipping and delivery solutions across Europe.

Vinted connects millions of users across 20 markets and is supported by top-tier venture capital firms such as Accel and Insight Partners.

Vinted Go has connected more than 40 carriers and more than 200,000 PUDO points across Europe to support the delivery of millions of parcels per year. The Vinted Group, composed of Vinted Marketplace and Vinted Go, is headquartered in Vilnius, with workplaces in Germany, Lithuania, France, the United Kingdom, and the Netherlands, employing over 2,000 people.

&nbsp;

About the Business Operations Manager Position

As Business Operations Manager, you will be responsible for ensuring that the PUDO point lifecycle - acquisition , deployment , activation , finance and partner support processes run smoothly - using automation and well-structured data to enable fast, reliable scaling.

You’ll be part of the Business Operations Excellence function, working at the intersection of Sales, Deployment, Maintenance, Network Performance, Operations, Finance, Product and Partner Support. The team’s mission is to build and maintain the systems, integrations, and cross-functional workflows that keep the full point lifecycle running efficiently. You will collaborate closely with stakeholders across these teams and act as a key owner of process design and system reliability.

&nbsp;

In this position, you’ll

• Lead technical maintenance and optimization of HubSpot (incl. workflows, automation, data structure), including other business development-related tooling, such as Zapier, DocuSign, Huboo, FROGED, etc.;

• Build up automated flows and integrations between systems, using Python, webhooks, and APIs to improve speed and quality in PUDO point lifecycle processes;

• Monitor system performance and integration health, proactively resolving issues and preventing process bottlenecks;

• Maintain and continuously improve the internal knowledge base, ensuring key operational processes and automations are clearly documented, up to date, and easy for teams to use;

• Work with cross-functional teams to create, manage, and document processes such as point churn and point billing,

&nbsp;

